      ],
      "status": "not-run"
    }
  ],
  "criteria": [
    {
      "id": "P02-AC01",
      "text": "macOS, Linux, and WSL installations boot without an LLM or hosted Jev connection."
    },
    {
      "id": "P02-AC02",
      "text": "An outside plugin can subscribe only to permitted kernel information and cannot publish commands or writes into the kernel."
    },
    {
      "id": "P02-AC03",
      "text": "Bad configuration, occupied ports, unavailable broker, and failed protected plugin produce actionable bounded failures."
    },
    {
      "id": "P02-AC04",
      "text": "Surrounding plugin failure does not corrupt boot state. Ordinary runtime communication uses NATS after bootstrap."
    },
    {
      "id": "P02-AC05",
      "text": "The existing launcher, environment selection and failure diagnostics remain available while the new boot path is opt-in. Both paths pass their defined startup and shutdown comparisons without sharing ownership of a live task."
    },
    {
      "id": "P02-AC06",
      "text": "LOCAL-01 cold launch starts the selected local Compose stack and waits for broker persistence and application readiness. Warm launch reuses the same instance without recreation or lost state. macOS, Linux and WSL fixtures pass without an LLM or Jev."
    },
    {
      "id": "P02-AC07",
      "text": "Simultaneous launches and a crashed startup owner converge on one owned instance. Wrong Docker context, conflicting ports, incompatible versions and partial startup produce bounded, specific diagnostics without deleting volumes, starting a shadow stack or attaching to another user."
    },
    {
      "id": "P02-AC08",
      "text": "The same versioned status response follows successful start and reuse. It includes instance identity/version, selected profile and endpoint, readiness, persistence health and authorized hub information with freshness. Missing or unimplemented services are labeled unavailable, never healthy."
    }
  ],
